{
 "_about": "Sound recipes for tools/audio/synth.py (lane B4), one entry per sound. Layers: noise {band [lo, hi] Hz, tilt dB/octave, env, lfo}, sweep {f0, f1, glide, harmonics, env} (a falling tone: booms, thuds), partials {freqs, decays, gains, hits [[t, gain]]} (ringing metal), hum {f, harmonics, wobble, grit} (motors). env = {attack, hold, decay} in seconds (decay is the exponential time constant). reverb {time_s, mix, lowpass, predelay_s}. variants = takes with small random differences (jitter). loop = cross-faded to repeat seamlessly. Output assets/audio/review/synth/<id>_<n>.wav. volume_db sets the sound's level in the mix, in the order of real loudness (57 mm muzzle blast about 170 dB SPL at the gun, a Juggernaut footstep about 115): every take is peak-normalised, so without it a footstep plays as loud as the cannon (it did, lane B4). Loops (servo, skid, winch) are levelled live in scripts/audio/mech_sounds.gd.",
